efins\u0097Americas; Olefins and Polyolefins\u0097Europe, Asia, International; Intermediates and Derivatives; Advanced Polymer Solutions; and Technology. The company produces and markets olefins and co-products, such as ethylene, aromatics, propylene and butadiene; polyolefins; polyethylene; polypropylene homopolymers and copolymers; propylene oxide and derivatives; oxyfuels and related products; and intermediate chemicals, such as styrene monomer and acetyls. It also produces and markets compounding and solutions, including polypropylene compounds, engineered plastics, masterbatches, and engineered composites and colors. In addition, it develops and licenses chemical and polyolefin process technologies; and manufactures and sells polyolefin catalysts and serves food packaging, home furnishings, automotive components, and paints and coatings applications. LyondellBasell Industries N.V. was incorporated in 2009 and is headquartered in Rotterdam, the Netherlands.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Peter Z. E. Vanacker | CEO & Executive Director | Age 59 | Compensation: $3.7M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 18K people. Revenue per employee of $1.6M ranks in the top quartile among Basic Materials peers. Each employee generates $20K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $5K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["LyondellBasell Industries NV is a large-cap basic materials business with a $20.8B market cap on $30.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -16% over the past three years and -1% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 13% against a 8% cost of capital, a 5-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $384M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 1 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 7.1\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin -0.9\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 9.4% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 20% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 379% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":3.785078024914373},{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Basic Materials peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins softening -1.1pp YoY \u2014 early warning on the moat","sev":"amber","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Operating margins 11% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 68/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; structural revenue/margin decline \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Trade policy and tariff whiplash \u2014 materials producers are first-order casualties of protectionist swings, and margin gets squeezed from both input and output pricing.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["14 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Technical Reactions to LYB Trends in Macro Strategies","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/21/Technical_Reactions_to_LYB_Trends_in_Macro_Strategies_111226100802_1794496082.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794496082.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.888,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Can LyondellBasell (NYSE:LYB) Steady Its Dividend as Prices Slip?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/dividend/can-lyondellbasell-nyselyb-steady-its-dividend-as-prices-slip","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794465060.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.402,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"Is LyondellBasell (NYSE:LYB) Leaning on Cash Discipline?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/dividend/is-lyondellbasell-nyselyb-leaning-on-cash-discipline","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794461340.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.402,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"LyondellBasell (LYB) Stock May Still Look Cheap Despite Refinery Sale","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/lyondellbasell-lyb-stock-may-still-161225853.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794413545.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.904,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Is LyondellBasell Industries (LYB) Undervalued After Its Return To Profit?","sour